1
00:00:06,932 --> 00:00:19,581
[SPEAKER_00]: Anurāḍa Sutta, he said, he's asking, what is the exalted deliverance of mind and what is the immeasurable deliverance of mind?

2
00:00:19,601 --> 00:00:27,166
[SPEAKER_00]: An exalted, here it bequeathed by and resolved upon an area the size of the roots of one tree, pervading it as exalted.

3
00:00:27,346 --> 00:00:29,448
[SPEAKER_00]: This is called an exalted deliverance of mind.

4
00:00:30,428 --> 00:00:32,470
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he goes on further, two or three trees,

5
00:00:34,443 --> 00:00:47,733
[SPEAKER_01]: The point being, even the smallest, as a root of a tree, basically, you start exalting your mind, literally, on the phenomenon that's larger than your body, that is present right here, right now.

6
00:00:48,154 --> 00:00:50,535
[SPEAKER_01]: Larger than your body, but related to your body.

7
00:00:51,736 --> 00:00:56,700
[SPEAKER_01]: Not just through your body being seated at the root of the tree, but also being composed of four great elements.

8
00:00:58,322 --> 00:00:58,562
[SPEAKER_01]: So,

9
00:00:59,888 --> 00:01:00,328
[SPEAKER_01]: It's enough.

10
00:01:00,449 --> 00:01:10,696
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not here to exalt your mind to the casinos of earth and so on, but it's enough just a room, just a floor that's wider than you, so to speak.

11
00:01:10,736 --> 00:01:11,277
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, kuti.

12
00:01:11,697 --> 00:01:12,358
[SPEAKER_01]: Kuti.

13
00:01:13,178 --> 00:01:29,191
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, again, if you make it personal, if you see that that kuti is composed of the four great elements that compose this very body, because of which you can think, feel, intend, decide, just do anything, well, because of which you exist, really.

14
00:01:30,301 --> 00:01:35,706
[SPEAKER_01]: And you recognize, yeah, the kuti or the root of the tree, it will come to destruction.

15
00:01:35,766 --> 00:01:37,608
[SPEAKER_01]: It will come to a deformation.

16
00:01:39,189 --> 00:01:42,052
[SPEAKER_01]: What is to be said for this body that's inferior to that?

17
00:01:43,312 --> 00:01:45,413
[SPEAKER_01]: That's going to happen even sooner, even quicker.

18
00:01:45,773 --> 00:02:11,361
[SPEAKER_01]: So, just the knowledge of that, you don't have to then destroy the tree to prove it to yourself, or destroy this body to prove it to yourself, which would be a contradiction in terms, obviously, but just the knowledge that it's a subject to destruction, that pertains to you, to your body, to your center, to the center of your world, which is this physical body, it's enough for dispassion and for not regarding that body as yours, not taking it up, not appropriating it.

19
00:02:15,972 --> 00:02:22,497
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's also a kind of, well, also a kind of training to enlarge in the mind.

20
00:02:23,377 --> 00:02:25,439
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, to establish it on a greater phenomenon.

21
00:02:25,639 --> 00:02:27,981
[SPEAKER_00]: But I've seen two different things at once.

22
00:02:28,261 --> 00:02:29,422
[SPEAKER_01]: What establishment is?

23
00:02:29,522 --> 00:02:32,324
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't mean you just start thinking about the roots of the trees or villages.

24
00:02:32,964 --> 00:02:43,072
[SPEAKER_01]: It means there has to be that dependence established, that connection between the presence of the phenomenon of the greater kind

25
00:02:44,004 --> 00:02:46,766
[SPEAKER_01]: In relation to the phenomenon of this body right here, right now.

26
00:02:47,446 --> 00:02:51,989
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not just enough to think about mountains and elements or whatever else.

27
00:02:52,149 --> 00:02:54,010
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to think it in relation to this body.

28
00:02:54,050 --> 00:02:54,891
[SPEAKER_01]: And what is the relation?

29
00:02:54,931 --> 00:03:09,240
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the simultaneous presence of these very four great elements that are comprising all these mountains, all these trees, this whole country, this church, including this body, these senses, these fleshy organs, because of which I am that which I think I am.

30
00:03:11,163 --> 00:03:26,128
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all of that, my whole world can be swept away and it is undermined through a simple possibility of being swept away by these great elements, by the matter that's out of your control.

31
00:03:26,788 --> 00:03:34,650
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if that changes, if that decides, if your heart decides to stop, for whatever reason, you don't know what's floating around your veins, you might block it.

32
00:03:34,770 --> 00:03:36,931
[SPEAKER_01]: Just, like, there you go.

33
00:03:37,111 --> 00:03:39,932
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, even these things that pertain to your body would be enough

34
00:03:42,051 --> 00:03:53,277
[SPEAKER_01]: To recognize that you have absolutely no say in the operation of the organs and the fleshy senses, sense organs, because yet your whole world is known as your world because of that.

35
00:03:54,078 --> 00:03:58,440
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when they go, your world cannot remain, not even for a second.

36
00:04:02,943 --> 00:04:06,965
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure, like, you can establish your mind on those greater things, like, say,

37
00:04:08,555 --> 00:04:26,368
[SPEAKER_00]: Me walking in the village, me in the village surrounded by the mountains, and so on, and have that mountain range as my... as far as my body is going, while I'm not losing sight of my body, my situation.

38
00:04:26,888 --> 00:04:27,309
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

39
00:04:27,489 --> 00:04:28,229
[SPEAKER_01]: It's within that.

40
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:28,850
[SPEAKER_00]: Within that.

41
00:04:28,970 --> 00:04:31,192
[SPEAKER_01]: It's simultaneously present within that.

42
00:04:32,096 --> 00:04:32,796
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the whole point.

43
00:04:32,817 --> 00:04:34,618
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not... it's not one and two.

44
00:04:34,738 --> 00:04:35,939
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like one within one.

45
00:04:36,219 --> 00:04:38,180
[SPEAKER_01]: But do I have to think about that?

46
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:38,861
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

47
00:04:38,901 --> 00:04:39,581
[SPEAKER_01]: No, that's the thing.

48
00:04:39,901 --> 00:04:42,763
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you have to think about it when the mind is not established upon it.

49
00:04:43,323 --> 00:04:43,564
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

50
00:04:44,084 --> 00:04:51,549
[SPEAKER_01]: When the mind gets established upon it, because it's through... look, your body is within that, which means, through your body, you can see that.

51
00:04:52,309 --> 00:04:59,054
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, your body, the presence of the elements of your body, keep your mind established upon the greater

52
00:05:00,077 --> 00:05:07,523
[SPEAKER_01]: phenomenon of those elements, which is the mountains, which is the mountain range, which is the... or on the other side, there's the perceptions of the forest.

53
00:05:08,304 --> 00:05:11,707
[SPEAKER_01]: Your mind is established in that, because forest is greater than the little village.

54
00:05:13,388 --> 00:05:15,910
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your mind is established upon the perceptions of the forest.

55
00:05:15,930 --> 00:05:18,412
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you go in a village, nothing can beset you there.

56
00:05:27,358 --> 00:05:29,620
[SPEAKER_01]: But, as I said, it needs to be made personal.

57
00:05:30,061 --> 00:05:36,407
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not an abstract pondering on, you know, the composition of the rocks or the mountain range or something.

58
00:05:36,427 --> 00:05:40,992
[SPEAKER_01]: It's basically seeing your body within that and seeing that through your body.

59
00:05:46,005 --> 00:05:57,913
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in the same sense, on top of the mountain range, there are trees being being swung by the wind, there's rolling rocks, there are, I don't know, crumbling dust of soil or whatever else.

60
00:05:58,854 --> 00:06:04,657
[SPEAKER_01]: On a more particular level, dead elements, yeah, your nails are growing, your body's moving around, you're sweating.

61
00:06:04,998 --> 00:06:06,699
[SPEAKER_00]: The rising of the water in the river.

62
00:06:07,305 --> 00:06:08,666
[SPEAKER_01]: Rising the water of the river, yeah.

63
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:10,488
[SPEAKER_01]: Passing the water out from your body.

64
00:06:10,788 --> 00:06:11,088
[SPEAKER_01]: Just...

65
00:06:12,029 --> 00:06:12,329
[SPEAKER_01]: It is.

66
00:06:12,850 --> 00:06:14,131
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the elements moving.

67
00:06:14,711 --> 00:06:23,858
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you start seeing your body as pertaining to that, that will result eventually in you not regarding your body as pertaining to you.

68
00:06:30,464 --> 00:06:31,845
[SPEAKER_00]: Because I was...

69
00:06:31,865 --> 00:06:34,927
[SPEAKER_00]: I wasn't really going into that contemplation, that kind of contemplation.

70
00:06:35,168 --> 00:06:35,588
[SPEAKER_00]: I was more...

71
00:06:36,127 --> 00:06:44,592
[SPEAKER_00]: Just expanding the mind for my body there, around it, within this, you know, as far as it's going.

72
00:06:44,872 --> 00:06:50,335
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is to learn how to keep seeing it within your body.

73
00:06:50,355 --> 00:07:05,043
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you're moving, as that sutta says, when you establish the mind upon the perception of the forest, when you go into the village and you see sights, you see things that would usually provoke lust or anger or so on, you wouldn't, because the mind remains established upon the perceptions of the forest.

74
00:07:06,114 --> 00:07:11,939
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't want to have to just, oh, I must sit motionless, cross-legged, for three hours, to practice this.

75
00:07:12,019 --> 00:07:20,446
[SPEAKER_01]: You might start like that, without distractions, but the point of that establishment is to disregard your body, regardless of the posture, regardless of its activity.

76
00:07:22,828 --> 00:07:26,832
[SPEAKER_01]: Not just to have the establishment when you're seated and motionless, because that wouldn't be really an establishment.

77
00:07:28,413 --> 00:07:34,398
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when your body is seated, lying down, standing up, or walking, the mind remains established upon the Great Phenomenon.

78
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:37,621
[SPEAKER_01]: That's basically your body is within that already.

79
00:07:39,902 --> 00:07:40,442
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's the thing.

80
00:07:40,462 --> 00:07:42,763
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the discernment that your body is already within that.

81
00:07:43,323 --> 00:07:44,784
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't need to fabricate anything.

82
00:07:44,804 --> 00:07:48,145
[SPEAKER_01]: You just have to discern it right now, because it is already there.

83
00:07:54,407 --> 00:08:00,370
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, it's the actual sutta after that, uh, upakālī, mārjupakālī.

84
00:08:02,823 --> 00:08:10,109
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Buddha's questioning Anuradha, and he says, eh... how do you abide in meditation?

85
00:08:10,790 --> 00:08:18,936
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, Venerable Sir, as we abide here, diligent, ardent, resolute, we perceive both light and a vision of forms.

86
00:08:21,038 --> 00:08:25,782
[SPEAKER_00]: Soon afterwards, the light and the vision of forms disappear, but we have not discovered the cause for that.

87
00:08:28,444 --> 00:08:31,407
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, well, I remember that being listed there, and

88
00:08:33,352 --> 00:08:34,652
[SPEAKER_01]: There are lots of notes on Pāli.

89
00:08:35,393 --> 00:08:35,833
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

90
00:08:35,853 --> 00:08:42,515
[SPEAKER_01]: So that translation, which you're reading out now, has quite a good chance of being very subject to that.

91
00:08:45,495 --> 00:08:51,117
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to get a few different translations, the actual Pāli as well, and then work on it.

92
00:08:52,357 --> 00:08:53,438
[SPEAKER_01]: But go on, read the whole thing.

93
00:08:53,538 --> 00:08:53,818
[SPEAKER_01]: Let's see.

94
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:05,482
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Buddha replies, you should discover the cause for that.

95
00:09:07,663 --> 00:09:17,769
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, before my enlightenment, while I was still only an unenlightened bodhisattva, I too perceived both lights and a vision of forms.

96
00:09:17,809 --> 00:09:26,234
[SPEAKER_00]: Soon after the light and the vision of forms disappeared, I thought, what is the cause and condition why the light and the vision of forms have disappeared?

97
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:28,255
[SPEAKER_00]: And I considered thus doubts arose in me.

98
00:09:29,498 --> 00:09:34,960
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, sometimes, he says, he sees... they see just light, and it just forms both

99
00:09:59,812 --> 00:10:02,073
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, it's like the whole light and thought.

100
00:10:03,394 --> 00:10:03,934
[SPEAKER_01]: Light and thought.

101
00:10:03,954 --> 00:10:04,915
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, what is the parliament?

102
00:10:04,935 --> 00:10:06,116
[SPEAKER_01]: Who has to stand there?

103
00:10:06,136 --> 00:10:14,681
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, I mean, you know, he was translating, what was it?

104
00:10:15,922 --> 00:10:17,322
[SPEAKER_01]: Non-indicative consciousness.

105
00:10:17,462 --> 00:10:19,484
[SPEAKER_01]: The concept of non-indicative, I recall.

106
00:10:19,984 --> 00:10:23,066
[SPEAKER_01]: He was translating consciousness that it's luminous all around.

107
00:10:23,686 --> 00:10:24,607
[SPEAKER_01]: And what did that mean?

108
00:10:26,018 --> 00:10:33,723
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when it comes to this thing of lights and visions or forms, I think there might be different connotations that would probably make more sense.

109
00:10:34,904 --> 00:10:38,967
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why I'm saying you have to look at all of them.

110
00:10:39,287 --> 00:10:44,511
[SPEAKER_00]: It seems that you can see separation, you can see forms, you can see light.

111
00:10:45,632 --> 00:10:46,733
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, in a way, yes.

112
00:10:47,193 --> 00:10:47,433
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

113
00:10:47,733 --> 00:10:52,677
[SPEAKER_01]: Because any form of

114
00:10:54,048 --> 00:11:06,757
[SPEAKER_01]: Manifestation of phenomenon, even as a thought, requires its... well, its arising, its manifestation, which means there is a degree of light in it, in regard to it.

115
00:11:07,537 --> 00:11:16,003
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if there is no degree of light in regard to it, Jesus would not be discerned against... against the nothingness, against basically non-arising.

116
00:11:18,409 --> 00:11:29,936
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even if you think about, like, I don't know, something like fleeting movements, just movements, just nothing particular, but thoughts that ponder on the nature...

117
00:11:29,996 --> 00:11:34,899
[SPEAKER_01]: Even that is discerned, to an extent, to a very ambiguous extent, obviously.

118
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:38,622
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not clearly defined as the object of your senses.

119
00:11:39,418 --> 00:11:43,182
[SPEAKER_01]: But as I said before, no matter how remote these thoughts are, they are valid phenomena.

120
00:11:43,843 --> 00:11:45,324
[SPEAKER_01]: And as such, they have arisen.

121
00:11:45,985 --> 00:11:48,467
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, there is a degree of light in that.

122
00:11:48,788 --> 00:12:00,260
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's... Like, if your mind were to be established upon the degree of light in regards to anything and everything that arises, means you'd be established in regards to everything and anything that arises.

123
00:12:02,317 --> 00:12:14,120
[SPEAKER_01]: Very similarly, the Buddha did say that the ultimate, the highest of the all kāsinas is kāsina of consciousness, which is kāsina of a non- arising in regard to the arising.

124
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:21,882
[SPEAKER_01]: It's because of that... sorry, it's because of it that the arising is possible to be discerned.

125
00:12:21,902 --> 00:12:23,763
[SPEAKER_01]: So, consciousness is the ultimate negative.

126
00:12:24,463 --> 00:12:25,183
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't appear.

127
00:12:27,604 --> 00:12:31,205
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're always conscious of, or rather, things are conscious of.

128
00:12:33,537 --> 00:12:36,179
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I mean when I say consciousness is out there with a form.

129
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:37,340
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean...

130
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:39,922
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't mean it's... it's actually there like the form.

131
00:12:40,322 --> 00:12:42,024
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a completely separate, different thing.

132
00:12:43,205 --> 00:12:49,049
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's out there paired with that form on the same... well, on the same level that it's below your feet.

133
00:12:49,630 --> 00:12:57,496
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't even conceive entering it, or even thinking about it, because whatever you think, you're already conscious of.

134
00:12:57,856 --> 00:12:58,917
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where you're able to think it.

135
00:13:00,233 --> 00:13:05,114
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means consciousness and the matter, in regard to it, are kind of prerequisites.

136
00:13:12,316 --> 00:13:14,357
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even if you say...

137
00:13:14,437 --> 00:13:16,197
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, okay, think about darkness.

138
00:13:17,798 --> 00:13:19,658
[SPEAKER_01]: There is an element of light in regard to that.

139
00:13:20,178 --> 00:13:21,038
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I'm thinking.

140
00:13:21,059 --> 00:13:21,299
[SPEAKER_01]: That's...

141
00:13:21,459 --> 00:13:21,739
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

142
00:13:21,839 --> 00:13:26,280
[SPEAKER_01]: They're referring to that kind of... Yeah, that's very subtle, but imagine your mind gets

143
00:13:27,276 --> 00:13:43,880
[SPEAKER_01]: And yes, imagine, because through imagination, along the right lines, you will start getting a clearer picture, which means you will be able... well, it means your thoughts will be less and less of an abstraction, as we spoke before, and will become more valid representations of what it actually is.

144
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:48,721
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how this sermon happens.

145
00:13:51,941 --> 00:13:54,682
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if the mind, as I said, imagining the mind is

146
00:13:58,300 --> 00:14:12,329
[SPEAKER_01]: They were composed to such extent, the discernment of light in regard to things that have manifested, that are enduring, already manifested, just among anything that arises.

147
00:14:17,573 --> 00:14:20,855
[SPEAKER_01]: Because in a way, that all of that is because of that light in regard to it.

148
00:14:25,668 --> 00:14:33,434
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, obviously, the light, in regard to it, will not be discerned, if there is nothing that this light is shining on, so to speak.

149
00:14:33,935 --> 00:14:37,517
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, no, I don't like that, because it implies the direction.

150
00:14:37,577 --> 00:14:39,279
[SPEAKER_01]: Usually, people think, ah, the shining light.

151
00:14:39,339 --> 00:14:39,519
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

152
00:14:40,119 --> 00:14:40,660
[SPEAKER_01]: Let's say like this.

153
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:45,664
[SPEAKER_01]: The light will not be discerned, because the things that arise, well, will not reveal.

154
00:14:46,925 --> 00:14:48,266
[SPEAKER_01]: And thus, you will know there's light.

155
00:14:50,733 --> 00:14:52,494
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is no light without the things.

156
00:14:52,935 --> 00:14:53,175
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

157
00:14:53,335 --> 00:14:59,239
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't start assuming that the light is eternal and things are just being revealed by this massive torch.

158
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:01,620
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

159
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:04,562
[SPEAKER_01]: Light is to the extent of the things arising.

160
00:15:05,403 --> 00:15:06,764
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's not the things arising.

161
00:15:07,244 --> 00:15:10,186
[SPEAKER_01]: But it actually belongs to things more than it belongs to you.

162
00:15:10,907 --> 00:15:12,207
[SPEAKER_01]: Or rather, completely belongs to things.

163
00:15:12,628 --> 00:15:15,410
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense that matter is paired with consciousness.

164
00:15:15,510 --> 00:15:15,950
[SPEAKER_01]: Not you.

165
00:15:16,390 --> 00:15:17,551
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not paired with consciousness.

166
00:15:17,571 --> 00:15:18,552
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't have consciousness.

167
00:15:19,272 --> 00:15:20,253
[SPEAKER_01]: Matter is paired with it.

168
00:15:21,526 --> 00:15:30,854
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not... it's not... it's not even that the matter is conscious, or consciousness possesses matter.

169
00:15:30,914 --> 00:15:32,696
[SPEAKER_01]: No, it's just matter-consciousness.

170
00:15:33,196 --> 00:15:36,739
[SPEAKER_01]: Two entirely separate entities that are juxtaposed together.

171
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:40,403
[SPEAKER_01]: As a result of that juxtaposition, you have

172
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:43,211
[SPEAKER_01]: Your whole life, your whole experience of everything.

173
00:15:43,611 --> 00:15:45,672
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and that's why I mean there's always below your feet.

174
00:15:45,712 --> 00:15:49,733
[SPEAKER_01]: That juxtaposition, that's the ratio between matter and consciousness.

175
00:15:50,494 --> 00:15:54,355
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just, well, you can't even think it accurately.

176
00:15:55,856 --> 00:15:59,137
[SPEAKER_01]: Or rather, the only way to think it accurately is to stop assuming it entirely.

177
00:16:10,093 --> 00:16:13,955
[SPEAKER_00]: You were saying about, talking about movement, tension, movement.

178
00:16:14,835 --> 00:16:15,136
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

